description:
repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/selection-entropy.ts declares `const floor` twice — once at function scope and again inside the try block, where the inner one shadows the outer. The outer declaration is now dead: nothing between it and the try block reads `floor`. Remove the dead outer declaration.

Delete this exact line, which is the one at function scope immediately following the `limit` declaration:
  const floor = Number(p.entropy_floor ?? 0.5) || 0.5;

Keep the other, indented copy inside the try block exactly as it is:
    const floor = Number(p.entropy_floor ?? 0.5) || 0.5;
    const ceiling = Number(p.entropy_ceiling ?? 0.95) || 0.95;

Change nothing else. The file must still typecheck and the resolver must keep emitting overall_entropy, collapsed, never_converging, undifferentiated, entropy_floor and entropy_ceiling exactly as it does now.

